WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:01.439
He’s fearless.

00:00:01.439 --> 00:00:02.610
He’s eccentric.

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.859
He’s dedicated to the SCP Foundation’s
cause.

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:11.699
In a lot of ways, he’s more like a living
legend than a regular Foundation employee.

00:00:11.699 --> 00:00:17.270
His face, voice, gender, and even species
may sometimes change, but it’s impossible

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.840
to miss that ornate medallion resting against
his chest.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.820
That’s right, today we’re talking about
the infamous Dr. Bright.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:31.000
Can you think of many other researchers who’ve
been cross-tested with the dreaded SCP - 682

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.410
and lived to tell the tale?

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:37.079
Of course, there’s a special advantage Dr.
Bright possesses that most researchers don’t.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:43.090
It’s the medallion he’s never seen without,
and because of it, Dr. Bright can’t die.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.579
How is this possible, you ask?

00:00:45.579 --> 00:00:48.800
Because, in a sense, he is that medallion.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:54.330
Don’t worry - after this crash-course in
all things Dr. Bright - including his origin,

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.280
his present, and his future - you’ll be
a lot less confused.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.380
So, who is Dr. Jack Bright?

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:06.289
For starters, he’s a decorated researcher
of anomalies for the SCP Foundation - and

00:01:06.289 --> 00:01:11.149
unlike most other researchers, he’s uniquely
qualified for the job on the grounds that

00:01:11.149 --> 00:01:13.969
he himself is an anomaly.

00:01:13.969 --> 00:01:18.200
Just don’t bring this up when you’re talking
to him - it’s kind of a sore subject.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:23.700
Beyond that, who or even what Dr. Bright is,
can be a bit of a loaded question with an

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.009
answer that depends on who and when you ask.

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:31.149
What we’re presenting to you here is one
of the more popular versions of the Dr. Bright

00:01:31.149 --> 00:01:36.719
story, and the one most closely adhered to
by Dr. Bright himself these days.

00:01:36.719 --> 00:01:41.119
One of our biggest challenges to understanding
Dr. Bright is that he has been so prolific

00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:46.020
in his exploits and achievements within the
Foundation that when telling his story it’s

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.020
hard to know where to start.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:52.039
But as the saying goes, let’s begin at the
beginning.

00:01:52.039 --> 00:01:53.240
Starting with the Bright Family.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:57.200
“Bright” was a name that carried a lot
of weight around the Foundation even before

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.439
Jack Bright signed up for service.

00:01:59.439 --> 00:02:03.859
His parents, Dr. Adam and Evelyn Bright, were
both Foundation personnel.

00:02:03.859 --> 00:02:08.680
His siblings were incredibly numerous and
the ones we’re aware of are TJ Bright, Mikell

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:14.020
Bright, Claire Pierce, and a nameless sister
now known only as SCP - 321.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:19.890
Sadly, you’ll soon see that the story of
the Bright family is one of consistent tragedy

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:21.260
and strife.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:25.900
While the anomalization of Dr. Bright took
hold a little later on in his life, his brother

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:30.950
TJ was born anomalous, and was designated
as SCP - 590.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:36.170
TJ had the ability to heal any ailment with
a touch, with the cost being that he took

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.090
on those ailments himself.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:42.830
He’s now used as a tool for healing at the
Foundation, and he’s consistently bedridden

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:45.190
with the illnesses he takes on.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:49.900
Dr. Bright induced a mental state similar
to that of a three year old in TJ, likely

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:55.230
in hopes of reducing the mental burden placed
on his poor brother, and sadly, that burden

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:59.150
goes far beyond healing the illnesses of strangers.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:03.350
When Adam and Evelyn experienced a tragic
stillbirth, they desperately tried to get

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:04.350
TJ to help.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:10.260
TJ did manage to save her, partially, but
the result wasn’t human - and both he and

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:16.130
the daughter, which came to be known as SCP
- 321, were taken into Foundation custody.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:22.590
SCP - 321 was a highly regenerative and stretched-out
abomination that seemed to keep growing with

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:27.850
age, but Adam still saw it as his daughter,
and spent the rest of his life trying to negotiate

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.840
her freedom from the Foundation.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:34.550
When his request was denied as a researcher,
he climbed the ranks to personnel director.

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:39.000
When his request was denied there, he became
a site director, and then a member of the

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:43.569
O5 Council - all with the intention of getting
his daughter back.

00:03:43.569 --> 00:03:48.290
But that never happened, and the rest of the
Council had him assassinated for his trouble.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:52.069
There’s no reward for sentimentality at
the Foundation.

00:03:52.069 --> 00:03:55.430
The other two Bright siblings are believed
to be polar opposites.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:56.430
Mikell

00:03:56.430 --> 00:04:00.990
Bright is one of the Foundation’s best field
agents, known to some as Agent Cowboy.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:06.050
His dedication to the cause and incredible
aptitude at his job has led some to speculate

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:09.240
that he may even be on the O5 Council already.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:14.260
Claire Pierce, on the other hand, disagrees
with the actions of the Foundation on a fundamental

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:18.970
level - which is understandable given the
horrific things they’ve done to the Bright

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:19.970
Family.

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:24.729
She defected and became a member of the Serpent’s
Hand - a fringe group dedicated to blowing

00:04:24.729 --> 00:04:28.520
the lid on SCP Foundation secrets.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:34.580
This brings us to the man himself - Dr. Bright,
the most well-known member of this sprawling

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.580
family.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:41.009
Much like most of the rest of his family,
he too entered the employment of the SCP Foundation.

00:04:41.009 --> 00:04:46.490
He was a junior researcher, and a relatively
unremarkable one, until his fateful run-in

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:50.909
with a certain necklace labelled SCP - 963.

00:04:50.909 --> 00:04:57.370
But what is SCP - 963 and how exactly did
Dr. Bright come into contact with it?

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:02.069
It all started in a small apartment that was
raided by the Foundation due to supposed Occult

00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:03.069
activities.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:08.220
There they found a single body, cause of death
apparently from suicide, clutching the medallion

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.400
that would later be designated as SCP - 963.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:17.129
The walls in the apartment were covered in
ritualistic supernatural symbols, and a number

00:05:17.129 --> 00:05:20.710
of Occult books were also found near the deceased
man’s body.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:25.610
The Foundation gathered that the man was attempting
to perform some kind of magical ritual, but

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:29.250
had apparently failed, leading to his own
demise.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:34.240
The Foundation soon learned that the recovered
medallion appeared to be utterly indestructible,

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:39.330
and they placed it under the care of a junior
researcher - one Dr. Jack Bright.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:44.629
Dr. Bright studied the medallion for years,
with very little to show for it, until one

00:05:44.629 --> 00:05:50.490
fateful day when he was tasked with transporting
the medallion to a different area of the containment

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:51.490
facility.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:55.800
While Dr. Bright was carrying out his simple
transport task, he made a simple decision

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:01.300
that changed the entire course of his life
forever - He held the medallion in his bare

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:02.300
hand.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:09.710
He also happened to be walking past the containment
chamber of SCP - 076 - 2, aka Abel, just as

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:12.559
a containment breach was about to occur.

00:06:12.559 --> 00:06:16.990
Abel is an immortal, hyper-violent warrior
who can summon blades out of interdimensional

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:17.990
portals.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:22.350
Dr. Bright, following in the tradition of
Bright family bad luck, happened to be right

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.559
in the path of Abel’s rampage.

00:06:24.559 --> 00:06:29.249
The ensuing battle between Abel and the assembled
Mobile Task Forces and guards resulted in

00:06:29.249 --> 00:06:34.059
the destruction of the entire wing of the
facility, and Dr. Bright was cut down in the

00:06:34.059 --> 00:06:36.779
brawl by the warrior’s supernatural blades.

00:06:36.779 --> 00:06:41.960
It seemed like the story of Dr. Bright was
short and simple - cut down in his prime in

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.389
the line of duty.

00:06:43.389 --> 00:06:47.710
But a few days later, as several members of
D-Class personnel were cleaning up the mess

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:54.150
caused by the containment breach, one unlucky
D-Class - known as D1-113 - happened upon

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.360
the medallion that Dr. Bright had been holding
when he died.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:03.770
He leaned over and picked it up, and instantly
underwent a sudden and drastic change in personality.

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:09.770
D1-113 was now insisting that he was Dr. Bright,
and since this D-Class had no reason to even

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:14.349
know of the recently deceased researcher’s
existence, he was immediately brought in for

00:07:14.349 --> 00:07:15.710
an interview.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:20.330
After a brief evaluation, it seemed clear
that somehow this D-Class really did have

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:22.210
the exact mind of Jack Bright.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:23.210
But how?

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:29.139
Well, after some experimentation - including
from Dr. Bright himself - they found the answer.

00:07:29.139 --> 00:07:32.879
The medallion’s purpose was to act as a
kind of vessel for the consciousness of the

00:07:32.879 --> 00:07:34.780
person killed holding it.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:39.220
Its original creator had hoped to use it as
a way to attain immortality, and took his

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.889
own life in order to complete the ritual.

00:07:41.889 --> 00:07:43.439
This was a mistake though.

00:07:43.439 --> 00:07:47.659
The correct way to complete the ritual was
being killed by someone else while holding

00:07:47.659 --> 00:07:52.039
the medallion, something that had happened
to Dr. Bright by total accident.

00:07:52.039 --> 00:07:56.389
In a sense, he’d been given a second chance
at life, but this came with some anomalous

00:07:56.389 --> 00:07:57.589
side effects.

00:07:57.589 --> 00:08:03.430
As it turns out, coming into direct contact
with the necklace - now known as SCP - 963

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:05.529
- 1 - is a death sentence.

00:08:05.529 --> 00:08:09.919
It causes your mind to be totally wiped and
replaced with that of Dr. Bright.

00:08:09.919 --> 00:08:14.659
If the necklace is then removed, you become
a lifeless husk until the necklace is placed

00:08:14.659 --> 00:08:15.869
back onto you.

00:08:15.869 --> 00:08:20.999
If the medallion remains in contact with its
host for a period of thirty days, Dr. Bright’s

00:08:20.999 --> 00:08:26.190
consciousness becomes permanently bonded to
the body without any contact from the medallion.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:30.690
If the medallion then comes into contact with
someone else, even if a permanent version

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:36.500
of Dr. Bright is already inhabiting another
body, they too will be infused with his consciousness.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:41.890
That means that if Dr. Bright wanted to, he
could have multiple versions of himself existing

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:42.890
at once.

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:47.530
Initially, the anomaly that Dr. Bright had
become was treated with suspicion and fear

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:49.090
by the Foundation.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:53.770
They were dealing with an intelligent and
now immortal consciousness capable of replicating

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:55.960
an unlimited number of times.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:09:01.790
In theory, he could even place his consciousness
into dangerous SCPs and gain even more power.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:07.330
Dr. Bright was placed under strict rules - like
not being able to interact with certain anomalies,

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:12.060
and having his hosts killed and switched at
thirty day intervals to prevent him from building

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:13.720
replicas of himself.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.450
However, this caution proved to be misplaced.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:22.210
Dr. Bright was an extremely intelligent, loyal,
and devoted researcher for the Foundation,

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:26.690
and as a result, his restrictions were slowly
lifted by the O5 Council.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:32.090
Much like his father before him, Dr. Bright
rose through the ranks, becoming both a celebrated

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.550
researcher and a director of various sites
during different periods of time.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:41.460
While this may seem like a win-win scenario
for all involved, this is a slightly more

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:44.780
complex situation for Dr. Bright himself.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:50.190
In a routine psychological evaluation led
by Dr. Simon Glass, Dr. Bright shared feelings

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.820
of frustration about his current situation.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:56.710
He felt as though he was treated differently
compared to the other researchers and given

00:09:56.710 --> 00:10:00.660
less trust due to a situation he didn’t
choose to be in.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:06.900
But for Dr. Bright, the psychological effects
of having been fused to SCP - 963 - 1 actually

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:12.910
extends far beyond workplace frustrations
and the boredom and sadness of un-asked for

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.350
immortality.

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:19.080
In a conversation with Level 1 Researcher
Dr. Frederick Heiden, Bright told him that,

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:24.040
in a sense, he truly was the heart of the
Foundation rather than just one small part

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.040
in it.

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:29.910
When asked to elaborate, he said that, because
of the gift and curse of immortality, he would

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:35.060
go on to outlive all the other human operatives
working for the SCP Foundation.

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:39.990
He would remain with the organization for
generations to come, perhaps centuries even,

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:45.650
and in that sense would be the one constant
from now until the Foundation meets its end.

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:50.090
When all else is gone, only Dr. Bright will
remain.

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:54.740
Of course, this is just an overview and we’ve
only just scratched the surface of Dr. Bright’s

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:58.950
actions and activities across the SCP Foundation
multiverse.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:03.610
But for now, all you need to know is that
Dr. Bright is still out there, and he’ll

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:08.120
be carrying that doomed name long after everyone
else with it has fallen.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:12.040
Whether that’s a good or bad thing, is up
to you to decide.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.440
Now go check out “SCP - 082 - Fernand the
Cannibal” and “SCP - 4000 - Taboo” to

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.190
get your Foundation fix from SCP Explained!

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:17.190
But why stop there?

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:18.420
Want to access some of the SCP Foundation’s
greatest secrets, but don’t know where to

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:19.420
start?

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:20.420
Subscribe to SCP Explained and turn on notifications
- we’re your guide to the strangest anomalies

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:21.389
and darkest corners of Foundation lore so
subscribe now!

